1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,296
Let me show you Demo Studio by using the real application.

2
00:00:03,439 --> 00:00:06,818
It helps you turn a working app into a narrated video you can send

3
00:00:06,960 --> 00:00:09,874
to testers, without asking them to install the app first.

4
00:00:10,328 --> 00:00:12,632
Here, I'm preparing the SoHelpMe demonstration.

5
00:00:12,775 --> 00:00:16,247
I load its project, which gives the video a name, keeps the

6
00:00:16,389 --> 00:00:19,479
application address handy, and brings in the scene plan.

7
00:00:19,621 --> 00:00:22,153
You can save that project and reuse it later.

8
00:00:22,607 --> 00:00:26,110
Each scene says what to show, what to say, and how long to allow.

9
00:00:26,252 --> 00:00:28,319
I review the refrigerator story here.

10
00:00:28,461 --> 00:00:31,820
The script describes what the actual app does, including the

11
00:00:31,962 --> 00:00:33,977
observation about two bottles touching.

12
00:00:34,431 --> 00:00:37,924
Next, I use free Piper narration, right on this computer.

13
00:00:38,066 --> 00:00:41,962
No Microsoft service, subscription, or API key is needed.

14
00:00:42,104 --> 00:00:44,719
Demo Studio measures the speech for caption timing.

15
00:00:44,861 --> 00:00:46,142
Listen before continuing.

16
00:00:46,285 --> 00:00:48,124
I've shortened the processing wait here.

17
00:00:48,578 --> 00:00:52,267
You can capture an application tab, or import an existing screen

18
00:00:52,409 --> 00:00:52,967
recording.

19
00:00:53,110 --> 00:00:56,861
I'm importing the real SoHelpMe interaction we just recorded.

20
00:00:57,003 --> 00:00:59,855
The preview lets me check the picture before I create the finished

21
00:00:59,998 --> 00:01:00,525
video.

22
00:01:00,979 --> 00:01:03,913
This is the point to check framing and private details.

23
00:01:04,056 --> 00:01:07,166
Optional crop controls and fixed black masks are available.

24
00:01:07,308 --> 00:01:10,491
Once the picture looks right, I confirm the preview and continue.

25
00:01:10,945 --> 00:01:13,136
Now I create the narrated preview.

26
00:01:13,278 --> 00:01:17,060
Demo Studio combines the recording, spoken narration, and captions

27
00:01:17,203 --> 00:01:19,393
into an MP4 on this computer.

28
00:01:19,536 --> 00:01:23,969
After reviewing it, I choose Export MP4 to save the finished file.

29
00:01:24,423 --> 00:01:28,298
Here is the resulting SoHelpMe video playing inside Demo Studio.

30
00:01:28,440 --> 00:01:32,336
It contains the real refrigerator conversation, practical replies,

31
00:01:32,478 --> 00:01:34,224
Piper narration, and captions.

32
00:01:34,367 --> 00:01:38,066
You can watch the separate MP4 at full size and share it with

33
00:01:38,209 --> 00:01:38,901
testers.

34
00:01:39,355 --> 00:01:43,035
For ThinkAgain or Waiting Room Buddy, change the app address and

35
00:01:43,195 --> 00:01:45,401
story, then repeat these steps.

36
00:01:45,561 --> 00:01:49,300
The finished watch page lets you play either demo full screen or

37
00:01:49,460 --> 00:01:50,911
download its MP4.

38
00:01:51,071 --> 00:01:53,219
Starting one video pauses the other.

39
00:01:53,379 --> 00:01:55,701
Your copyright notice appears at the bottom.

40
00:01:55,861 --> 00:01:57,022
You're ready to share.
